  },
  "segment_count": 192,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 10.07,
      "end": 10.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Welcome back. In this session, we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 10.08,
      "end": 12.35,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "going to tackle initial value problem y."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 12.36,
      "end": 15.43,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "+ ty = 2t. And this initial value"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 15.44,
      "end": 16.99,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "problem is going to be subject to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 20.03,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "initial condition y of 0 = 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 20.04,
      "end": 25.55,
      "duration": 5.51,
      "text": "We are going to use the method of"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 34.63,
      "end": 34.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And what I want you to use is both"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 34.64,
      "end": 41.95,
      "duration": 7.31,
      "text": "definite integrals"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 52.95,
      "end": 52.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, why don't you take a few minutes to"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 52.96,
      "end": 55.03,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "think about the problem and we will be"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 55.04,
      "end": 60.87,
      "duration": 5.83,
      "text": "right back."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 63.95,
      "end": 63.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, welcome back. So, I hope that you"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 63.96,
      "end": 64.91,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "worked out the first part of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 64.92,
      "end": 67.79,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "problem. So, what are we going to do to"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 67.8,
      "end": 70.35,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "solve this ODE? First, we need to review"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 70.36,
      "end": 72.07,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "what what is the method of integrating"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 72.08,
      "end": 73.19,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 73.2,
      "end": 74.23,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 74.24,
      "end": 75.51,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 75.52,
      "end": 76.99,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "when we use the integrating factor,"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 77.0,
      "end": 83.95,
      "duration": 6.95,
      "text": "basically we're trying to write down"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 86.71,
      "end": 86.72,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "our ODE in a different form by"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 86.72,
      "end": 90.07,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "introducing a function u."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 90.08,
      "end": 92.63,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "And the goal is to find the function u"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 92.64,
      "end": 94.55,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "such that we can rewrite this left-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 94.56,
      "end": 96.35,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "side"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 96.36,
      "end": 100.07,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "as the derivative of the product y.u."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 100.08,
      "end": 102.83,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "So, in this case, if we're looking at"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 102.84,
      "end": 104.71,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "identifying the function u that would"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 104.72,
      "end": 106.47,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "give us this form,"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 106.48,
      "end": 107.71,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "y"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 107.72,
      "end": 109.39,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "u."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 109.4,
      "end": 112.03,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "We need to just basically identify that"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 112.04,
      "end": 116.35,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "this is u."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 119.23,
      "end": 119.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And from previous sessions, we saw that"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 119.24,
      "end": 121.63,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "this would give us classical"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 121.64,
      "end": 126.27,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "uh classical solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 127.83,
      "end": 127.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "that involves"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 127.84,
      "end": 130.95,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "an exponential of the integral of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 130.96,
      "end": 136.19,
      "duration": 5.23,
      "text": "right-hand side after dividing by u."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 138.95,
      "end": 138.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Which gives us exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 138.96,
      "end": 140.95,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "of t squared over 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 140.96,
      "end": 142.87,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "So, the integrating factor is just using"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 142.88,
      "end": 144.31,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "a trick so that we simplify our"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 144.32,
      "end": 146.19,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "left-hand side and write it in the form"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 146.2,
      "end": 149.27,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "of the derivative of a product y.u. So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 149.28,
      "end": 151.67,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "now we identify our integration factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 151.68,
      "end": 155.47,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "It's u equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 157.79,
      "end": 157.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "exponential of t squared over 2. Now, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 157.8,
      "end": 159.95,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "can go back to our equation and I'm"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 159.96,
      "end": 163.03,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "going to just label it with a star here."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 163.04,
      "end": 166.11,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "So, now this equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 166.12,
      "end": 167.43,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "is written"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 167.44,
      "end": 173.55,
      "duration": 6.11,
      "text": "in this form."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 176.63,
      "end": 176.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "t And the integral of just basically"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 176.64,
      "end": 178.91,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "derivative is itself. So, if we use"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 178.92,
      "end": 181.19,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "first the approach of"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 181.2,
      "end": 183.19,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "definite integrals, actually we're going"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 183.2,
      "end": 184.59,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "to switch the order and I'm going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 184.6,
      "end": 187.23,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "start with indefinite integrals first."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 187.24,
      "end": 188.19,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 188.2,
      "end": 190.23,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "using indefinite integrals, we'll be"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 190.24,
      "end": 197.47,
      "duration": 7.23,
      "text": "integrating both sides."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 204.11,
      "end": 204.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we will just be left with"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 204.12,
      "end": 205.35,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "y.u."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 205.36,
      "end": 207.07,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "Remembering that u is just exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 207.08,
      "end": 208.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "of t squared over 2. On the right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 209.0,
      "end": 212.15,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "side, we're just integrating"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 212.16,
      "end": 214.59,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "t exponential of t squared over 2. And"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 214.6,
      "end": 215.79,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "here you can recognize that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 215.8,
      "end": 217.47,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "derivative of exponential of t squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 217.48,
      "end": 219.79,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "over 2 would have t in front of it. So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 219.8,
      "end": 220.99,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "this is actually very simple"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 221.0,
      "end": 225.39,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "integration."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 227.15,
      "end": 227.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "But we are"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 227.16,
      "end": 228.63,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "in the case of a differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 228.64,
      "end": 231.51,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "where we need a constant of integration."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 231.52,
      "end": 233.39,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And again here, we would end up with two"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 233.4,
      "end": 235.07,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "constants of integration on both sides,"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 235.08,
      "end": 236.35,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "but given that we're dealing with a"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 236.36,
      "end": 238.11,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "first-order differential equation, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 238.12,
      "end": 241.27,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "can regroup that in one constant."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 241.28,
      "end": 243.75,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "And then we can just find our solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 243.76,
      "end": 246.91,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "by dividing this equation by u."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 246.92,
      "end": 248.79,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And u, if you remember, is just"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 248.8,
      "end": 250.75,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "exponential of t squared over 2. So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 250.76,
      "end": 252.87,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "it's equivalent to multiplying both"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 252.88,
      "end": 254.95,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "sides by exponential of minus t squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 254.96,
      "end": 255.99,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "over 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 256.0,
      "end": 257.63,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 257.64,
      "end": 266.55,
      "duration": 8.91,
      "text": "I'm just going to write it down."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 268.55,
      "end": 268.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Which then just gives us exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 268.56,
      "end": 270.35,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "minus t squared over 2 multiplied by"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 270.36,
      "end": 272.27,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "exponential of t squared over 2, which"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 272.28,
      "end": 273.99,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "is 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 274.0,
      "end": 275.07,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "And"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 275.08,
      "end": 277.75,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "c exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 277.76,
      "end": 280.63,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "of minus t squared over 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 280.64,
      "end": 283.39,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "So, that's our solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 283.4,
      "end": 284.91,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "But remember that we're trying to solve"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 284.92,
      "end": 286.67,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "an initial value problem that is subject"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 286.68,
      "end": 288.99,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "to an initial condition. And our initial"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 289.0,
      "end": 293.71,
      "duration": 4.71,
      "text": "condition is y of 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 296.51,
      "end": 296.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "equals to 3. Which means that here y of"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 296.52,
      "end": 298.67,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "0 would give us exponential to 0, which"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 298.68,
      "end": 301.87,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "is just a constant. So, we end up with"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 301.88,
      "end": 304.71,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "3 equals to 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 304.72,
      "end": 308.31,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "plus c. Therefore,"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 308.32,
      "end": 310.43,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "c is equal to 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 310.44,
      "end": 312.03,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "And the final form of the solution would"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 312.04,
      "end": 314.79,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "just be 1 + 2 exponential of minus t"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 314.8,
      "end": 316.15,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "squared over 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 316.16,
      "end": 317.51,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "So, we started with the indefinite"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 317.52,
      "end": 319.71,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "integral. So, what if we would do this"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 319.72,
      "end": 332.99,
      "duration": 13.27,
      "text": "using definite integrals?"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 335.03,
      "end": 335.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, we don't need to start from the"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 335.04,
      "end": 336.63,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "beginning. We just need to take the"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 336.64,
      "end": 341.31,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "problem a few steps before when we"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 341.32,
      "end": 347.31,
      "duration": 5.99,
      "text": "integrated both sides of the equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 349.23,
      "end": 349.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And here, specify the bounds of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 349.24,
      "end": 351.31,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "integral. So, how do we want to specify"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 351.32,
      "end": 352.87,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "the bounds of the integral? We're given"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 352.88,
      "end": 354.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "an initial condition that is at t equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 354.8,
      "end": 358.35,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "to 0. So, that's what we want here."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 358.36,
      "end": 362.51,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "And we're integrating to the variable t."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 362.52,
      "end": 364.11,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "But one thing is important when you do"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 364.12,
      "end": 365.55,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "that is that you have the variable t"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 365.56,
      "end": 367.99,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "that is in the bounds of the integral."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 368.0,
      "end": 371.03,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "So, we want the integrand to not be"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 371.04,
      "end": 372.43,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "written"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 372.44,
      "end": 374.67,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "in terms of the variable of integration."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 374.68,
      "end": 377.35,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "And so, it is very important to change"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 377.36,
      "end": 380.63,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "the label"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 387.47,
      "end": 387.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "That's how you proceed for definite"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 387.48,
      "end": 388.71,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "integrals."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 388.72,
      "end": 390.99,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "So, in this case, then we end up with"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 391.0,
      "end": 395.11,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "similar"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 399.39,
      "end": 399.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, u of y u.y evaluated at t"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 399.4,
      "end": 402.87,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "minus u.y evaluated at 0. And from our"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 402.88,
      "end": 404.63,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "initial conditions and the form of u, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 404.64,
      "end": 406.91,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "know the value of this of this side of"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 406.92,
      "end": 409.19,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "this term in the equation. And here,"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 409.2,
      "end": 411.15,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "we're just again recognizing that this"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 411.16,
      "end": 413.75,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "is just the derivative of exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 413.76,
      "end": 418.31,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "to the s squared over 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 420.59,
      "end": 420.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "evaluated between"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 420.6,
      "end": 422.71,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "0 and t."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 422.72,
      "end": 425.55,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "Okay? So, here if I just carry on with"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 425.56,
      "end": 427.59,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "the right-hand side and then go back to"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 427.6,
      "end": 429.55,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "left-hand side in the next step, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 429.56,
      "end": 432.03,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "would end up here with just t squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 432.04,
      "end": 433.43,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "over 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 433.44,
      "end": 437.07,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "minus 1. Exponential of 0 is 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 437.08,
      "end": 438.63,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "And now, let's deal with this left-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 438.64,
      "end": 441.19,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "side. So, again,"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 441.2,
      "end": 443.19,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "we end up"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 443.2,
      "end": 446.43,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "with u.y minus u.y evaluated at 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 446.44,
      "end": 448.43,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "However, u of 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 448.44,
      "end": 449.75,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "is just"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 449.76,
      "end": 452.03,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "the function exponential to t squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 452.04,
      "end": 455.35,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "over 2 evaluated at 0, which is 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 455.36,
      "end": 457.19,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "And y of 0,"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 457.2,
      "end": 459.03,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "we have it cuz that was our initial"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 459.04,
      "end": 462.31,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "condition. And this is only 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 462.32,
      "end": 465.07,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "So, we have u.y minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 465.08,
      "end": 467.99,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "1.3, which is just basically minus 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 468.0,
      "end": 469.39,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "And on the right-hand side, we have"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 469.4,
      "end": 472.51,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "exponential of t squared over 2 minus 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 472.52,
      "end": 476.59,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "Which gives us"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 479.83,
      "end": 479.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "exponential of t squared over 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 479.84,
      "end": 482.47,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "minus 1. Now, bring in this minus 3 on"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 482.48,
      "end": 485.67,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "the other side, we now have a plus 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 485.68,
      "end": 488.67,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "All of this multiplied by 1 over u,"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 488.68,
      "end": 491.43,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "which was our exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 491.44,
      "end": 494.19,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "of minus t squared over 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 494.2,
      "end": 495.75,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "And therefore, we end up with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 495.76,
      "end": 497.19,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "similar"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 497.2,
      "end": 498.83,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "uh solution that we had for the definite"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 498.84,
      "end": 504.03,
      "duration": 5.19,
      "text": "integral. 3 minus 1 is just 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 506.43,
      "end": 506.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, we have minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 506.44,
      "end": 508.67,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "t squared over 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 508.68,
      "end": 510.27,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 510.28,
      "end": 514.95,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "1."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 518.11,
      "end": 518.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, using both the definite integrals"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 518.12,
      "end": 519.709,
      "duration": 1.589,
      "text": "approach and the indefinite integrals,"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 519.719,
      "end": 522.19,
      "duration": 2.471,
      "text": "we recovered the same results. And the"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 522.2,
      "end": 524.19,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "main point of this problem was really to"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 524.2,
      "end": 526.47,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "practice using the integration factor"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 526.48,
      "end": 528.79,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "and practice using both approaches with"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 528.8,
      "end": 531.11,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "the definite and indefinite integrals."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 531.12,
      "end": 533.59,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "So, uh this ends the problem and I'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 533.6,
      "end": 536.44,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "see you next time."
    }
